{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For from the rising of the sun</b> — from the edge of the earth to the edge of the earth, such is the inhabited world, and in every place I have commanded — they would offer Me something esteemed: incense would be presented before Me, and a pure grain offering. Or מוקטר there is like קטורת, and they would heed My voice to magnify My great name. Afterward the rabbi the sage told me a very correct interpretation of this verse, and it adheres to the matter: for the prophet, concerning the contempt and the blemish with which they profane the Name, therefore he says: for in all the inhabited world, from the rising of the sun to its setting, great is My name among the nations and esteemed, and in every place in the world, this matter is considered in eyes — that they honor and magnify My name — as though in every place they bring before Me for My name everything incensed and presented that is fitting for My honor." "<b>And a pure grain offering</b> — not as you do, to present before Me bread that is blemished, blind, and lame, and sick, and it is not evil in your eyes. And why do you not take to heart: great is My name among the nations, and you profane it."], :book :malachi, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Resolved 'הרב החךם' generically as 'the rabbi the sage'; identity of the interlocutor is not specified."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Malachi -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/malachi"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:11.705626268Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}